00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:36.340
Richard Bair: anything… I mean, not anything, there's limits to what they could do. They can't touch count 800 or 801 and things like that. But I mean, you know, I mean, they could… they could take all the nodes off the network and things like that. So, we don't have to worry about it from that perspective. And from a performance perspective, they execute, you know, there's a handful of these transactions every month, so…

111
00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:44.940
Richard Bair: The sort of… the size and all that kind of stuff is far larger at, you know, just with jumbo Ethereum transactions.

112
